  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 226 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThrough early next week (Monday)...\n\nThrough midweek (Wednesday): RAP/water vapor analysis indicates \nupper low is situated over the southeast this morning and 595DM\nmid level ridge over the Desert Southwest, leading to mean \nnortherly dry flow across the Gulf Coast states. This will lock \nin PWs generally around one inch and low humidity aloft (i.e. \n700-300mb layer humidity in the low teens to single digits) and \nefficient mixing. This leads to moderating temperatures: \nhighs becoming seasonably warm into Wednesday (91F to 96F) and\nseasonable lows (68F to 71F this morning to 71F to 74F Wednesday\nnight). With afternoon mixing being the norm, heat stress will\nremain lower, with a gradual uptick of heat index in southwestern\nareas (heat indices in the 102F to 105F range by tomorrow\nafternoon).\n\nLate week into early next week (Thursday through next Monday):\nAs the upper low weakens the grip over the Southeast into\nThursday, low level southerly return flow and an uptick in\nmoisture (low and deep layer moisture) will favor less efficient\nmixing, warmth/moist advection and increasing heat stress late\nweek through the weekend. Temperatures will be seasonably warm\n(highs in the 92F to 96F range and lows in the 72F to 76F range).\nThe region will remain in more of a large scale weakness in the\nflow but low level flow will help moderate in higher surface\ndewpoints (70F to 76F) and increasing heat stress concerns.\n\nEven though large scale pattern is somewhat similar to what we \nhave been observing, the key difference is the low level return \nmoist advection and increased deepening moisture aloft (PWs in the\n1.5 to 2 inch range by the weekend into early next week). Rain \nchances will mainly be summertime variety (diurnally induced) with\nisolated to at times scattered coverage (20 to 40 percent range).\nThis pattern will not favor any noteworthy storm threat, but a \nfew scattered stronger gusty storms with locally heavy rain cannot\nbe ruled out, especially later into the weekend.\n\nMain hazard weather concern remains increasing heat stress into \nthe weekend. This still remains several days out, with most \nlikely areawide concerns from Friday onward. Holding off mention \nin HWO this forecast cycle, but will likely get a point of needing\nHWO graphics and heat headlines. /DC/",
